  "title": "Colombia and Nepal Earthquake: Over 100 Dead Amid 7.4-Magnitude Strike",
  "summary": "A powerful 7.4-magnitude earthquake struck western Colombia, causing over 100 deaths and significant damage to major cities like Cali and Pereira, with authorities responding by calling for rescue efforts and coordinating with neighboring countries. A 32-year-old woman was rescued after 36 hours following the quake. A flash flood in Nepal and a landslide in Upper Subansiri district resulted in five Army personnel missing and four people dead, while a similar event in Tibet saw 469 deaths in Nepal and three in Tibet.",
